# L1 batch 1: regions r001-r070 (protocol v1.2.1; L0 batch-05 convention on X parts with modality-split P/R applies)
# r001-r002 .claude/INSTRUCTION_MAP.md
SPLIT R:EXTRA-L1-0012 | a: Every instruction artifact is placed by stability (0-core, 1-architecture, 2-technology, 3-project). | b: Every artifact starts with a one-line header (Level, optional Capability/Facet, Owns, Scope, Loading). | c: Conformance dependencies point only to the same or a more stable level. | d: Core and Architecture name no concrete implementation technology in any form, pointers included, except the fixed vocabulary (.NET, C#, TypeScript, Git, HTTP; ASP.NET Core and NuGet not exempt), and refer to Level 2 only by role, capability, facet or a technology-neutral skill name. | e: Every artifact is listed in the instruction map. | f: check-instructions is run after any instruction-system change.
SD P:EXTRA-L1-0012 R:EXTRA-L1-0012#a | S: instruction artifact placement M: MUST both E: none in either T: none
SD P:EXTRA-L1-0014 R:EXTRA-L1-0012#b | S: instruction artifact headers M: ENFORCED (P) = checker-enforced MUST (R) (F7) E: none in either T: none
SD P:EXTRA-L1-0010 R:EXTRA-L1-0012#c | S: conformance dependencies M: ENFORCED (P) = checker-enforced MUST (R) (F7) E: none in either T: none
SD P:EXTRA-L1-0011 R:EXTRA-L1-0012#d | S: Core and Architecture artifacts M: ENFORCED (P) = checker-enforced MUST (R) (F7) E: fixed platform vocabulary (both) T: none
SD P:EXTRA-L1-0015 R:EXTRA-L1-0012#f | S: instruction-system changes M: MUST both E: none in either T: after any change
CX X:BF-L1-0068 | The instruction map imposes four stability levels, technology-neutral vocabulary in Core/Architecture, one-line artifact headers and a checker run after every change.
RD OVERLAP X:BF-L1-0068 R:EXTRA-L1-0012 | R: the level model the finding summarizes.
RD COMPOUND_PART R:EXTRA-L1-0013 P:EXTRA-L1-0013 | R adds slot cardinalities, selection resolution and cleared-slot semantics.
